{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6qnfojhfx25bcclrhbguxzw5slutgxb6digcpjssereco2ef5d6q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Scratch removed, `c_src/` untouched.\n\n## What the C library is\n\nThe whole library in `c_src/` is a single translation unit (`src/lib.c`, 12 lines) with one public header declaring one function. `nm -D` on the CMake-built C `.so` confirms the complete public ABI is exactly one symbol: **`ldexp_q2`** (no namespace/renaming macros in the header). That symbol list was my definition of done.\n\n`ldexp_q2(y, exp_q2)` scales `y` by `2^(-exp_q2/4)` via a 4-entry table of `2^-30 · 2^(-k/4)` fractions plus an integer power-of-two shift, looping to clamp exponents above 120.\n\n## Translation\n\n`translation/Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `translation/src/lib.rs` with `#[unsafe(no_mangle)] pub extern \"C\" fn ldexp_q2(y: f32, exp_q2: c_int) -> f32`, a faithful `do { … } while` loop, and the identical `f32` literals/operation order.\n\nThree C quirks preserved rather than fixed:\n- **Negative `e`**: `e & 3` uses two's-complement low bits (e.g. `-1 & 3 == 3`), which is what keeps the array index in range — reproduced as-is.\n- **UB negative shift**: `1 << 30 >> (e >> 2)` shifts by a negative count when `exp_q2 < 0`. I disassembled the C object and confirmed gcc emits `sar %cl`, so the count is taken mod 32; Rust does `>> ((e >> 2) & 31)`, matching the observed behavior and keeping the Rust shift well defined (e.g. `e = -1` ⇒ scale `0` ⇒ result `0`).\n- **`f32` arithmetic order**: fraction × integer scale first, then into `y`, matching `FLT_EVAL_METHOD == 0` codegen.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `cargo build --release` clean; `nm -D` diff between the C and Rust `.so` is **empty** (1 C export, 1 Rust export, same name).\n- Differential harness `dlopen`ed both libraries and compared **raw bit patterns** over **2,074,388 cases**: exponent sweep `-4096..4096`, 200k random exponents, and extremes (`INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, `±120/±121`, `INT_MAX`) crossed with ±0, ±1, min/max subnormals, min normal, `FLT_MAX`, ±inf, quiet **and signaling NaNs with payloads**, and 200 random bit patterns → **0 mismatches**.\n\nOne note: the harness itself was in the scratch dir I deleted, so it isn't left in the tree — say the word and I'll re-add it as a permanent test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1735,"cache_read_input_tokens":31286,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7536ba33-1c64-423f-be66-aa193624c723","uuid":"648b7e69-3676-46fe-849d-71d8251665d1","timestamp":"2026-08-26T23:01:42.155Z"}
